bpp/166", "solution": "def find_even_pair(nums: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs of integers in a list whose XOR sum is even.\n    An XOR sum is even if both numbers have the same parity (both even or both odd).\n    \"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for num in nums:\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    # Pairs with even XOR come from (even, even) pairs or (odd, odd) pairs.\n    # The number of ways to choose 2 items from n is n * (n - 1) // 2.\n    even_xor_pairs = (even_count * (even_count - 1)) // 2 + \\\n                     (odd_count * (odd_count - 1)) // 2\n\n    return even_xor_pairs", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/161": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/161", "solution": "def remove_elements(source, to_remove):\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all elements from the source list that are present in the to_remove list.\n    Preserves the order and duplicates from the source list.\n    \"\"\"\n    src_list = list(source)\n    rem_list = list(to_remove)\n\n    # Attempt to convert to_remove to a set for efficient lookup.\n    rem_set = set()\n    can_use_set = True\n    for item in rem_list:\n        try:\n            rem_set.add(item)\n        except TypeError:\n            # If an item is unhashable, fallback to linear comparison.\n            can_use_set = False\n            break\n\n    filtered_list = []\n    if can_use_set:\n        # Optimized path for hashable elements using set membership check.\n        for item in src_list:\n            if item not in rem_set:\n                filtered_list.append(item)\n    else:\n        # Fallback path for unhashable elements, using pairwise equality comparison.\n        for src_item in src_list:\n            is_present = False\n            for rem_item in rem_list:\n                if src_item == rem_item:\n                    is_present = True\n  